# FIELD-WINTER: FIELD_Barn_Winter = FIELD_Barn under the world's snow layer (Common/WeatherSnow.glslh): the scene's
# collection WP_Winter names the CC0 ambientCG Snow010A albedo / normal / ARM as Texture world parameters and
# SnowCover 0.9; the look is the scan, the code only places it by the up-facing normal (owner 10-29).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn_Winter.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject selection set SunElevation 25
Дано --subject selection set SunAzimuth 110
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,170,2500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.25,-1
Тогда-вид 1_winter_eye barn, trees, fence and bales in frame (imported mesh sources re-imported from their glTF, no stale-cache error); barn roof white, not grey; snow lies on the branches as a layer, not specks; walls and trunks bare; blades poke out of the snow; editor.log errors 0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,900,2500
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.15,-1
Тогда-вид 2_winter_high the whole field white under snow to the horizon, Terrain Far included, no sharp snow edge at grazing distance; barn and trees visible, roof white, wall faces dark and bare, no black patches
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position -300,2221,-3600
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.53,-0.51,-0.7
Тогда-вид 3_winter_tree Tree 1 from 25 m above and aside: the crown's upper half white with snow as one layer (canopy normal baked in island_tree_01.gltf), its underside and the trunk dark
